# Line endings
#
# Git normalizes text files to LF in the index, but with core.autocrlf=true —
# the Windows default, and what this machine is set to — it checks them back
# out as CRLF. Prettier's `endOfLine` default is "lf", so it then reports every
# file in the repo as unformatted: 209 of them, none for a reason anyone could
# see in a diff. Formatting the files does not fix that on its own, because the
# next clone re-introduces CRLF.
#
# Pinning the working tree to LF makes `format:check` give the same answer on a
# Windows dev machine and on Linux CI. It changes no committed content — the
# index was already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
